# Accepted CRITICAL vulnerabilities (Trivy baseline), Person B quality gate.
#
# The SCA (stage 2) and image scan (stage 6) jobs fail on any CRITICAL vulnerability that has a fix
# available, EXCEPT the ones listed here. Every entry is a reviewed decision:
#   - why it is accepted, and who approved it (the pull request that added it)
#   - an expiry date (exp:): after that date Trivy reports it again and the
#     build fails until the decision is reviewed and renewed or the issue fixed.
# Process: docs/exemption-process.md. New entries need the other team member's
# approval in the pull request review.

# jsonwebtoken 0.1.0 and 0.4.0: JWT verification bypass (alg: none).
# Deliberate Juice Shop vulnerability (JWT forgery challenges). Upgrading to
# 9.x changes the API used by lib/insecurity.ts and express-jwt 0.1.3. The
# exploit path is closed in code by Person A's fix/jwt-alg-none (every token is
# verified with RS256 using Node's crypto). Approved in the quality gates PR.
CVE-2015-9235 exp:2027-01-31

# lodash 2.4.2: prototype pollution in defaultsDeep.
# Pulled in only by sanitize-html 1.4.2, which Juice Shop pins on purpose for
# its XSS challenges; lodash 4 breaks sanitize-html 1.x. Risk accepted for the
# training app. Approved in the quality gates PR.
CVE-2019-10744 exp:2027-01-31

# tar 6.2.1: denial of service via a crafted gzip bomb.
# Nested copy used only by sqlite3 5.1.7 (which declares tar ^6) and its
# native-build tooling, at install time; the application never extracts
# user-supplied archives (the top-level tar is already 7.5.x). Forcing tar 7
# into sqlite3 risks breaking the native module install. Revisit when sqlite3
# moves to tar 7. Approved in the quality gates PR.
CVE-2026-59873 exp:2027-01-31
